00:09:00.581 --> 00:09:01.580
I do it all the time.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.532
It's why I love Q an A,

00:09:02.532 --> 00:09:03.693
it's why I love public speaking,

00:09:03.693 --> 00:09:05.412
it's why I don't have a set presentation.

00:09:05.412 --> 00:09:07.641
I'm reading the room in real time.

00:09:07.641 --> 00:09:08.939
I'm reading my staff.

00:09:08.939 --> 00:09:13.154
It's how I scale my
ability to read at scale.

00:09:13.154 --> 00:09:14.617
Like walking through the
12th floor and be like,

00:09:14.617 --> 00:09:15.771
that person's in trouble.

00:09:15.771 --> 00:09:17.949
It's weird, kind of like I don't
even like talking about it.

00:09:17.949 --> 00:09:20.770
It's like a really nice
innate skill that has helped

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.358
me scale my personality.

00:09:23.928 --> 00:09:26.539
I, for some reason, feel
those feelings in people's

00:09:26.539 --> 00:09:28.409
comments and tweets.

00:09:28.409 --> 00:09:30.394
Now, maybe it took me a long
time to get the cadence.

00:09:31.744 --> 00:09:34.074
Of course, there's been times
where I've maybe read into

00:09:34.074 --> 00:09:36.790
it wrong because context and tone is lost,

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.618
but I've go to tell you,

00:09:38.618 --> 00:09:41.735
my intuition is if you go
hardcore in trying to do that

00:09:41.735 --> 00:09:45.137
through Twitter, through
your Facebook comments

00:09:45.137 --> 00:09:46.252
on your posts,

00:09:46.252 --> 00:09:48.306
and this is more about me
reading people responding to my

00:09:48.306 --> 00:09:51.263
